Interesting, I am back and I have implemented the loop thing. It now loops infinitely whenever the --loop flag is passed or loop=True is manually set in AnimationToASCII. What happened was the two KeyboardInterrupt's were clashing with each other, so whenever one wanted to quit print_to_term's KeyboardInterrupt fired which stopped a frame but didn't stop the whole animation, so the animation couldn't be stopped. The fix was to introduce a special if self.loop condition in print_to_term that does NOT check for KeyboardInterrupt in case of looping inside print_to_term, and only checks it in display(). I think this is good for a commit now.

